# The Build 7 box token. Copy to `deploy/ccrc-mail.token` (gitignored, never
# committed), REPLACE THE LINE BELOW with a real value, and `deploy.sh` ships
# it to BOTH boxes:
#   fleet host  -> ~/.cc-secrets/ccrc-mail.token   (notify.sh + every session)
#   server box  -> ~/.ccrc/mail.token              (read at boot)
#
# Mint with:  openssl rand -hex 32
#
# This authenticates THE BOX, not a session: every fleet session runs as one
# UNIX user and can read the file. Per-session identity is attribution
# (`{fromId, fromUuid}` checked against the registry), and the spec says so.
#
# Both boxes' readers (coord/token.ts, notify.sh) take the first line here
# that is neither blank nor a `#`-comment as THE TOKEN, so this file's shape
# — comments, then exactly one value line — already IS the deployable shape:
# a real value on the line below is enough, no other edit needed. DO NOT SHIP
# THE PLACEHOLDER BELOW AS-IS — it is committed to this public repo, so it
# authenticates nobody. If you instead DELETE the line below and ship only
# comments (or truncate the file to 0 bytes), both readers refuse to treat
# that as "unconfigured": a PRESENT file with no extractable value throws
# loudly at boot rather than silently opening the ingress (fix-round finding
# 4) — "never shipped a token" and "shipped an empty one" are different
# mistakes and must not read the same.
REPLACE-THIS-LINE-WITH-THE-OUTPUT-OF-openssl-rand--hex-32
